From fb94835eb8d9e07200466a0e06da916ae58f1f6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viren070 <viren070@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:45:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ass_cache: share caches between threads

Lookups take no lock: a bucket's chain only grows while they run, with
new items going in at its head by compare-and-swap, and a thread that
finds an item another is still constructing waits for it. Each thread
records the items it uses in its own client, which ass_cache_flush()
moves to the back of the eviction order once the frame is done, and
items leave the cache only between frames. Destructors are split into
key and value ones, so a thread that loses the race to insert a key can
free its copy.
